From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weiyi Feng <fwy1998@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:21:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hosted: no platform nub for the NVRAM service

BeringiaPlatform keeps the whole device tree (empty exclude list), so
createNubs also met /options, which processTopLevel had replaced with the
IODTNVRAM stub, and made an IOPlatformDevice from it. That nub copied its
properties from the stub's dictionaryWithProperties(), which is NULL
without an NVRAM handler: the registry entry with no property table that
hosted patches 0017/0038 worked around and that softwareupdated finally
tripped over in serializeProperties (named by the previous patch:
IOPlatformDevice, registered from IODTPlatformExpert::createNubs). The
NVRAM service is not a platform device: do not make a nub of it.
---
 iokit/Kernel/BeringiaPlatform.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/BeringiaPlatform.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/BeringiaPlatform.cpp
index bb33c5d..c9841f9 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/BeringiaPlatform.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/BeringiaPlatform.cpp
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
  * IOPanicPlatform, so IOKit picks it instead of panicking with "Unable to find driver for this platform".
  */
 #include <IOKit/IOPlatformExpert.h>
+#include <IOKit/IONVRAM.h>
 #include <machine/machine_routines.h>
 extern "C" void sysctl_unblock_osenvironment(void);
 extern "C" {
@@ -56,6 +57,21 @@ public:
 	virtual const char * deleteList( void ) APPLE_KEXT_OVERRIDE { return ""; }
 	virtual const char * excludeList( void ) APPLE_KEXT_OVERRIDE { return ""; }
 
+	/*
+	 * processTopLevel has already put the NVRAM service (here the IODTNVRAM stub) in /options' place in the
+	 * device-tree plane, so createNubs meets it among the root's children. It is not a platform device, and a nub made
+	 * from it copies its properties from the stub's dictionaryWithProperties(), which is NULL: an IOPlatformDevice
+	 * with no property table, which faulted in getProperty, dictionaryWithProperties and serializeProperties in turn.
+	 * (The generic excludeList skips "options" by name, but the stub no longer has a name property to match.)
+	 */
+	virtual IOService * createNub( IORegistryEntry * from ) APPLE_KEXT_OVERRIDE
+	{
+		if (OSDynamicCast(IODTNVRAM, from)) {
+			return NULL;
+		}
+		return IODTPlatformExpert::createNub(from);
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * The number of CPUs normally reaches the kernel from the CPU interrupt controller the ACPI platform sets up
 	 * (IOCPUInterruptController::initCPUInterruptController -> ml_set_max_cpus). Until Beringia has its own IOCPU
